    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> did not accept its claim to continue the Socialist Federal Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a>: Security Council Resolution 777 treated it as a new state, and it joined the United Nations only in 2000.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanctions">Sanctions</a> imposed during the Yugoslav Wars brought hyperinflation of the Yugoslav dinar between 1992 and 1994, reaching 313 million percent, the third worst hyperinflation in history.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosovo">Kosovo</a> War of 1998–1999 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a>'s bombing ended with Kosovo under a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> mission, and the Bulldozer Revolution of 2000 removed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slobodan-milosevic">Slobodan Milošević</a> from power.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Barred from international competition by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanctions">sanctions</a>, the FR Yugoslav basketball team returned at the 1995 EuroBasket in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> and won it at its first tournament, beating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> 96–90 in the final.</p></aside>
    </section>

